      "writtenOn": "2025-03-14T12:02:55Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thank you for your quick response. We are developing a phone call app using your low-level audio library, Oboe, and we are experiencing an issue where users cannot change the call volume when the screen is locked. Probably this problem seems to affect many apps that utilize the VoiceComm audio profile. The Oboe team has confirmed this issue as well, using the official Google OboeTester app, as noted here:\n\nhttps://github.com/google/oboe/issues/2153#issuecomment-2638405101\n\nFrom my understanding, the VoiceComm volume change event should not be skipped, as users may need to adjust the call volume even when the screen is off, similar to how they can with music streams. For this reason, I have added a check for VoiceComm similar to the one for music streams.",
